+# HVE Engine 2.5 coding instructions
+
+Follow the repository-wide rules in `AGENTS.md` and the machine-readable
+contract in `docs/article_data_v2_5.json`.
+
+- Preserve the 32,400-state finite core and explicit canonical/legacy layouts.
+- Never change valid CR80 words when extending CR88 or later envelopes.
+- Treat CR88 as `[10-byte CR80][1-byte metadata]`, not as a dense rank.
+- Keep HVE2 `0x05` flags zero and CRC coverage payload-only.
+- Keep structural adjacency separate from perceptual conductance.
+- Use native-scale Oklab with `sigma=0.02/sqrt(2)` for
+  `hve-chi-oklab/v1`.
+- Keep color conversion external to graph adjacency and return a typed loss
+  status.
+- Update Python, C11, vectors, rejection tests, specification, and evidence
+  together for shared behavior.
+- Do not describe EFQ as quantum computation or declared RGB profiles as
+  measured device calibration.
+- Do not turn benchmark measurements into WCET or hard-real-time claims.
