 # Changelog
 
+## 2.5.0 — 2026-08-01
+
+- Added CR88 as an 88-bit physical envelope: unchanged ten-byte CR80 plus one
+  byte containing `color_space[7:6]`, `color_state[5:4]`, and four mandatory
+  zero reserved bits.
+- Added HVE2 profile `0x05` for heterogeneous per-state chromatic metadata,
+  with zero flags, exact `11N` payloads, and the existing payload-only
+  CRC-32/ISO-HDLC rule.
+- Distinguished the 80-bit raw CR80 rank, the 81-bit minimum of the navigable
+  profiled product, the 82-bit minimum of the transport-valid CR88 domain, and
+  the 88 physical transport bits.
+- Standardized `hve-chi-oklab/v1` on the unchanged structural RGB8 edge set,
+  with native-scale Oklab conductance and default
+  `sigma=0.02/sqrt(2)`.
+- Added typed external conversion among sRGB, Display-P3, and Adobe RGB (1998)
+  with `REJECT`, `CLIP`, and OkLCh local-MINDE mapping policies.
+- Added the mutually exclusive results `EXACT`, `QUANTIZED`, `OUT_OF_GAMUT`,
+  `CLIPPED`, and `MAPPED`; gamut is tested in target linear RGB before target
+  transfer encoding and quantization.
+- Added byte-identical Python/C11 CR88 conformance over 100,000 deterministic
+  pseudorandom vectors plus boundary and negative cases.
+- Published CR88, conversion, and three-vertex perceptual-Laplacian golden
+  vectors in `tests/golden_vectors_v25.json`.
+- Extended the separate CPython and strict C11 benchmarks to compare CR80 and
+  CR88, structural and perceptual diffusion, and typed conversion. Percentiles
+  remain host diagnostics rather than WCET or hard-real-time guarantees.
+- Clarified that standard-profile colorimetry is not measured physical-device
+  calibration and that Oklab is not a CIE standard.
+- Added the article-to-repository architecture contract, machine-readable
+  scientific data manifest, agent instructions, integration guide, and an
+  executable validator tying claims to code and preserved evidence.
+
