+### 8.8. CR88 heterogeneous envelope and HVE2 profile 0x05
+
+CR88 is an 88-bit physical envelope, not a new dense rank. Bytes `0..9` are
+the unchanged CR80 word. Byte `10` is
+
+```text
+color_space[7:6] | color_state[5:4] | RESERVED[3:0].
+```
+
+The two fields use the Control-128/v4 codes in Section 8.7. All four reserved
+bits MUST be zero. The CR80 carrier MUST be absent exactly for NoColor and
+present for valid or uncalibrated RGB. Every other state/space/carrier
+combination MUST be rejected.
+
+CR88 distinguishes `1+4*2^24=67,108,865` transport-valid chromatic values.
+Together with `G_ref`, that transport domain contains
+`2,536,135,276,406,400,000,000,000` values and has a minimum dense width of 82
+bits. The 88-bit envelope intentionally contains transport slack; CR80 remains
+an exact 80-bit rank.
+
+HVE2 profile `0x05` carries `N` concatenated CR88 words, has payload length
+`11N`, and requires frame flags equal to zero. CRC-32/ISO-HDLC covers only the
+payload, preserving the HVE2 rule. After header, length, and CRC validation, a
+decoder MUST validate every CR80 word, reserved metadata bit, and truth-table
+combination.
+
+### 8.9. Typed conversion between profile fibers
+
+`convert(color,target_space,policy)` is an external typed operator. It MUST NOT
+add an edge or alter the refined geometric coordinate. For a valid profiled
+RGB source, the ordered pipeline is source transfer decoding, normalized
+XYZ-D65, target linear RGB, target-gamut test, declared gamut policy, target
+transfer encoding, and nearest-integer RGB8 quantization. The gamut test MUST
+precede encoding and quantization.
+
+The policies are `REJECT`, `CLIP`, and `MAP_OKLCH_MINDE`. The result status is
+one of `EXACT`, `QUANTIZED`, `OUT_OF_GAMUT`, `CLIPPED`, or `MAPPED`.
+`OUT_OF_GAMUT` returns no target color. `MAPPED` may be emitted only by the
+declared nonlinear local-MINDE OkLCh mapper. Uncalibrated RGB has no source
+profile and MUST be rejected as conversion input; NoColor remains NoColor.
+
+Normative direction vectors and floating diagnostics are published in
+`tests/golden_vectors_v25.json`. The complete algorithm and claim boundary are
+in `docs/hve25_implementation_contract.md`.
+
