 This directory preserves the portable C11 implementation of the validated BASE,
 chromatic, refined, HVE-chi-Refined, serialization, and framing core. Version
-2.4 preserves CR80 and Control-128/v3, adds Control-128/v4, mandatory profiled
-CR80 frame flags, and the implicit structural chromatic topology. The dedicated
-`hve_chi_benchmark` executable measures encode and decode independently for all
-three words. The Python package remains the profile-aware colorimetry layer; no
-hard-real-time, energy, or C harmonic claim is made in this release.
+2.5 preserves CR80 and Control-128/v3/v4, adds CR88 and HVE2 profile `0x05`,
+implements the `hve-chi-oklab/v1` local conductance, and provides typed
+sRGB/Display-P3/Adobe RGB conversion with declared gamut policies. The
+dedicated `hve_chi_benchmark` executable measures CR80/CR88 encode/decode,
+structural/perceptual Laplacians, and conversion independently. No hard-real-
+time, energy, physical-device calibration, or C harmonic claim is made.
