+# HVE 2.5 implementation contract
+
+Status: normative extension profile
+
+Version: 2.5.0
+
+Date: 2026-08-01
+
+HVE 2.5 adds heterogeneous chromatic transport, a normative perceptual
+conductance profile, and typed color conversion to the HVE 2.4 structural
+core. It does not change `G_ref`, the pointed raw-color carrier, the mixed-radix
+rank, or any valid CR80 word.
+
+## 1. Preserved structural core
+
+The refined geometry remains
+
+```text
+G_ref = Z_(360*1080000) x Z_2 x Z_(5*1080000) x Z_9
+|G_ref| = 37,791,360,000,000,000.
+```
+
+The raw pointed carrier remains
+
+```text
+C* = {NoColor} disjoint_union RGB24
+|C*| = 1 + 2^24 = 16,777,217.
+```
+
+Consequently,
+
+```text
+X_(chi,ref) = G_ref x C*
+|X_(chi,ref)| = 634,033,847,445,120,000,000,000.
+```
+
+Its canonical mixed-radix rank is still exactly 80 bits wide at minimum and is
+still serialized as the ten network-order bytes of CR80. CR80 does not contain
+81 significant bits.
+
+The navigable profiled domain from HVE 2.4 is
+
+```text
+C_profiled = {NoColor} disjoint_union
+             ({sRGB, Display-P3, Adobe RGB (1998)} x RGB24),
+|C_profiled| = 1 + 3*2^24 = 50,331,649.
+```
+
+Its product with `G_ref` has
+`1,902,101,466,752,640,000,000,000` states and needs 81 bits in a hypothetical
+dense rank. HVE 2.5 does not define that hypothetical rank.
+
+## 2. CR88 heterogeneous envelope and HVE2 profile 0x05
+
+CR88 is an 88-bit physical envelope, not a dense rank:
+
+```text
+bytes 0..9: unchanged CR80 word
+byte 10:    color_space[7:6] | color_state[5:4] | RESERVED[3:0]
+```
+
+The metadata fields are:
+
+| Bits | Field | Codes |
+|---:|---|---|
+| 7..6 | `color_space` | 0 NONE, 1 sRGB, 2 Display-P3, 3 Adobe RGB (1998) |
+| 5..4 | `color_state` | 0 NoColor, 1 valid, 2 uncalibrated, 3 reserved |
+| 3..0 | `RESERVED` | MUST be zero |
+
+Four bits are allocated to chromatic metadata and four bits are reserved. A
+decoder MUST enforce this truth table:
+
+| `color_state` | `color_space` | CR80 carrier | Valid | Meaning |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| NoColor | NONE | absent, RGB=0 | yes | isolated pointed state |
+| valid | sRGB | present | yes | interpreted under the declared standard profile |
+| valid | Display-P3 | present | yes | interpreted under the declared standard profile |
+| valid | Adobe RGB (1998) | present | yes | interpreted under the declared standard profile |
+| uncalibrated | NONE | present | yes | RGB bytes with no source profile |
+| reserved | any | any | no | reserved state code |
+| any other combination | any | any | no | inconsistent metadata/carrier |
+
+The CR88 transport-valid chromatic carrier therefore contains
+
+```text
+1 + 4*2^24 = 67,108,865
+```
+
+distinguishable values: NoColor, three declared RGB fibers, and one
+uncalibrated RGB class. With `G_ref`, the transport-valid domain contains
+
+```text
+2,536,135,276,406,400,000,000,000
+```
+
+values and would require 82 bits if densely ranked. The difference between 82
+semantic-capacity bits and 88 physical bits is intentional transport slack;
+it does not alter the CR80 bijection.
+
+HVE2 profile `0x05` carries `N` concatenated CR88 words. Its payload length is
+exactly `11N` bytes, and its frame flags MUST be zero because profile metadata
+is already carried per word. The existing HVE2 checksum rule is unchanged:
+
+```text
+CRC-32/ISO-HDLC(CR88_0 || ... || CR88_(N-1)).
+```
+
+The CRC covers the payload only, not the 16-byte header. A conforming decoder
+performs checks in this order:
+
+1. validate magic, major version, profile, flags, count, and total length;
+2. identify the exact `11N`-byte payload;
+3. validate the payload CRC;
+4. validate the CR80 rank and metadata truth table of every word.
+
+## 3. Normative perceptual conductance profile
+
+The optional declared profile is `hve-chi-oklab/v1`. It never changes the
+structural edge set. Within one valid RGB profile fiber,
+
+```text
+u ~ v iff |r-r'| + |g-g'| + |b-b'| = 1.
+```
+
+NoColor remains isolated, uncalibrated RGB is not a navigable vertex, and
+colors in different profile fibers remain structurally disconnected.
+
+For each structural edge, both endpoints are converted from their declared RGB
+profile through normalized XYZ-D65 to Oklab. On the native Oklab scale,
+
+```text
+DeltaE_OK(u,v) = ||Oklab(u) - Oklab(v)||_2
+w(u,v) = exp(-DeltaE_OK(u,v)^2 / (2*sigma^2)).
+```
+
+The default is
+
+```text
+JND = 0.02
+sigma = 0.02/sqrt(2) = 0.01414213562373095,
+```
+
+so an edge whose `DeltaE_OK` is 0.02 has weight `e^-1`. Values such as
+`sigma=2.0` are not valid defaults on the native Oklab scale unless a separate
+hundredfold Delta-E rescaling is explicitly declared.
+
+The weighted local Laplacian is
+
+```text
+(L_chi,w f)(u) = sum_(v~u) w(u,v) * (f(u) - f(v)).
+```
+
+Because `w(u,v)=w(v,u)>0` on the unchanged undirected edges, the operator is
+symmetric, has zero row sums, and is positive semidefinite. The unweighted
+structural Laplacian remains independently available.
+
+## 4. Typed external conversion
+
+`convert(color, target_space, policy)` changes only the chromatic fiber. It
+does not create a graph edge, does not change the geometric state, and is not
+assumed to be injective or reversible.
+
+For a valid profiled RGB source, the pipeline is:
+
+```text
+encoded source RGB8
+-> decode source transfer curve
+-> normalized XYZ-D65
+-> target linear RGB
+-> gamut test in target linear RGB
+-> REJECT, CLIP, or MAP_OKLCH_MINDE
+-> encode target transfer curve
+-> round-to-nearest RGB8 quantization.
+```
+
+The gamut test MUST occur before target transfer encoding and quantization.
+Uncalibrated RGB MUST be rejected as a conversion source because no source
+transfer curve or primaries are declared. NoColor converts to NoColor with
+status `EXACT` and does not acquire RGB values.
+
+The result statuses are mutually exclusive:
+
+| Status | Required meaning |
+|---|---|
+| `EXACT` | in gamut and exactly represented on the target RGB8 grid, or identity/NoColor conversion |
+| `QUANTIZED` | in gamut, but target RGB8 rounding loses information |
+| `OUT_OF_GAMUT` | policy `REJECT`; no target color is returned |
+| `CLIPPED` | out of gamut; target linear channels were clamped to `[0,1]` |
+| `MAPPED` | out of gamut; the declared nonlinear gamut mapper was applied |
+
+The normative `MAP_OKLCH_MINDE` policy implements constant-lightness and
+constant-hue OkLCh chroma reduction with the CSS Color 4 local-MINDE binary
+search, `JND=0.02`, and `epsilon=0.0001`. `MAPPED` MUST NOT be emitted for an
+unspecified mapper, and gamut mapping MUST NOT be described as a single 3x3
+matrix.
+
+Normative direction vectors include:
+
+```text
+sRGB(255,0,0) -> Display-P3(234,51,35): QUANTIZED
+Display-P3(255,0,0) -> sRGB, REJECT: OUT_OF_GAMUT, no color
+Display-P3(255,0,0) -> sRGB, CLIP: (255,0,0), CLIPPED
+Display-P3(255,0,0) -> sRGB, MAP_OKLCH_MINDE: (255,11,12), MAPPED
+```
+
+The exact floating-point diagnostics and serialized words are published in
+`tests/golden_vectors_v25.json`.
+
+## 5. Colorimetric provenance and claim boundary
+
+The matrices and transfer curves are tied to the declared sRGB, Display-P3,
+and Adobe RGB (1998) standard profiles. XYZ and D65 are the profile connection
+basis; Oklab is the perceptual model adopted by the profile. Oklab is not a CIE
+standard, and the RGB-to-XYZ matrices are not generic "CIE matrices".
+
+Declaring a standard RGB profile is not physical device calibration. HVE 2.5
+does not ingest ICC profiles, measured primaries, spectral power distributions,
+viewing conditions, or observer-specific metamerism. It therefore provides
+profile-aware colorimetry and traceable loss diagnostics, not absolute
+device-calibrated perception.
+
+## 6. Conformance and measurement boundary
+
+A conforming implementation MUST provide:
+
+- CR88 encode/decode with strict reserved-bit, rank, carrier, and truth-table
+  rejection;
+- HVE2 `0x05` framing with zero flags, `11N` payload length, and payload-only
+  CRC-32/ISO-HDLC;
+- the unchanged structural graph and unweighted Laplacian;
+- `hve-chi-oklab/v1` with native-scale default sigma;
+- typed conversion with all five statuses and the three declared policies;
+- published positive and negative golden vectors;
+- independently measured CR80/CR88 encode and decode distributions.
+
+The reference validation includes 100,000 deterministic pseudorandom CR88
+vectors cross-checked byte-for-byte between Python and portable C11, plus
+boundary vectors and negative metadata cases. The full domain is not
+exhaustively enumerated; the raw CR80 bijection remains established by its
+mixed-radix inverse proof.
+
+Latency percentiles are host measurements. They are not energy measurements,
+WCET bounds, interrupt analyses, or hard-real-time guarantees.
+
+## 7. Primary colorimetric references
+
+- W3C, *CSS Color Module Level 4*: <https://www.w3.org/TR/css-color-4/>
+- Adobe Systems, *Adobe RGB (1998) Color Image Encoding*:
+  <https://www.adobe.com/digitalimag/pdfs/AdobeRGB1998.pdf>
+- Björn Ottosson, *A perceptual color space for image processing*:
+  <https://bottosson.github.io/posts/oklab/>
