+## CR88 and HVE2 profile 0x05
+
+CR88 is exactly 11 bytes per state:
+
+```text
+bytes 0..9  unchanged CR80
+byte 10     color_space[7:6] | color_state[5:4] | reserved[3:0]
+```
+
+The color codes are identical to Control-128/v4. The four low bits must be
+zero. NoColor requires `space=NONE` and an absent zero-RGB CR80 carrier; valid
+RGB requires a declared space and a present carrier; uncalibrated RGB requires
+`space=NONE` and a present carrier. All other combinations are rejected.
+
+HVE2 profile `0x05` contains `11*count` payload bytes and requires flags zero.
+Its CRC-32/ISO-HDLC covers those payload bytes only. CR88 has 88 physical bits;
+its unchanged CR80 prefix still has 80 bits, while the complete transport-valid
+domain would require 82 bits if densely ranked.
+
